            <!-- What to compare between car loan offers -->
            <div class="mt-12">
            <h3 class="qt-h3 mb-6">What to Compare Between Car Loan Offers</h3>
            <div class="qt-table-wrap">
                <table class="qt-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>What to check</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td class="font-semibold">Rate type and tenure</td><td>A fixed rate keeps the EMI steady. A longer tenure lowers the EMI but raises the total interest, so check both numbers.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="font-semibold">Processing and documentation fees</td><td>Charged once, usually with GST on top. Add them to the cost of the loan when comparing offers.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="font-semibold">Prepayment and foreclosure charges</td><td>RBI rules bar prepayment penalties on floating-rate loans taken by individuals for non-business purposes. Fixed-rate car loans can carry a foreclosure charge, so read the terms if you plan to close early.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="font-semibold">Amount financed</td><td>Lenders fund a share of the on-road or valuation price. A larger down payment lowers both the EMI and the total interest.</td></tr>
